cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MetaSpace Membrane — a deterministic safety membrane for machine-generated software"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Szőke"
    given-names: "László-Ferenc"
    email: "admin@metaspace.bio"
    affiliation: "MetaSpace.Bio Engine Project"
repository-code: "https://github.com/LemonScripter/metaspace-membrane"
url: "https://metaspace.bio"
abstract: >-
  MetaSpace Membrane turns an undecidable question — "is this AI doing the right
  thing?" — into a decidable one — "is this effect inside the declared boundary?" —
  and enforces the answer deny-by-default. One .bio constitution drives three
  membranes (capability, value-invariant, epistemic) and two products (an app
  membrane and an AI coding-agent membrane / Warden), each backed by reproducible
  proofs. Containment, not correctness. Patent pending.
keywords:
  - ai-safety
  - agent-safety
  - guardrails
  - capability-security
  - webassembly
  - deny-by-default
